Package: erhai-sensors
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Depends: @DEPENDS@, iio-sensor-proxy, systemd, udev
Conflicts: hexagonrpcd
Description: OnePlus Pad 2 Pro (erhai) accelerometer for screen rotation
 Connects the Qualcomm Sensor Core on the ADSP to the desktop: a private
 hexagonrpcd file server attaches the ADSP sensor domain and serves it the
 stock sensor configuration, libssc reads the accelerometer over QRTR, and a
 private iio-sensor-proxy build with SSC support replaces the distribution
 binary through a systemd drop-in. Distribution files are left unchanged;
 removing the package restores Ubuntu's iio-sensor-proxy at the next boot.
 .
 The per-unit sensor registry is not included. Import it once with
 erhai-sensors-import-registry from a copy of this tablet's Android persist
 data; until then the stack stays inactive. Only the accelerometer is
 exposed. This is an offline candidate: the mount matrix and the start-up
 sequence have not yet been validated on hardware.
